Z||000000||Little Duce Coupe||11-02-2001||04:39 PM||||<BR>The Fiero came with an "optional" rear window defogger.....why?  Once my coupe warms up the back window NEVER fogs up.<BR>Did get a bonus for selling them? Hhmmmm...<P>Did the engineer that designed where the spare tire goes work in a different department than the engineer that decided what size tires and rims they were going to put on the car?  Hhmmmm....<BR>OR<BR>IS THAT WHAT THE LUGAGE RACK WAS FOR!?! Hmmm..<P>Did the designer realize that because the engine is in the rear.... that the depth of water a Fiero can traverse is only limited to the speed of the car and the size of the drivers B#$'s. Hhmmmm....<P>Did the designers realize that although the little "plastic" car they designed would take greats amount of bad mouthing (still does) would set the industry standard for using materials other than metal in the skin of cars and for standardizing the skeletal framing model.<BR>Is that where Saturn got the idea.. Hhmmmm...<P>Will my little 88' classic red coupe actually turn into a "classic" in it's own right some day.  Hhmmmmm...... (I think so)<P>Hhmmmm... do you have any?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||10
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-02-2001||08:25 PM||||The rear window defogger clears the condensation from the window caused by snow melt on the rear deck and water dribbling onto hot exhaust manifold. From California, don't know snow.<P>A stock 215x15x60 tire fits nicely in an empty rear trunk compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||11-02-2001||09:42 PM||||Boomtastic wrote a wile ago:<P>Ever wonder why ...<P>.. GM used the largest 4 cylinder engine they were building in the base coupes, yet they used the smallest V6 engine they were building in their GTs?<P>.. GM installed manual windows in a car with a foot-wide center console?<BR>Did they really think that people would be able to lean over and reach the other handle?<P>.. GM made that extra area "cut out" on the left of the instrument cluster, just above the tach, and then left it un-used?<P>.. GM never installed a switch to leave the headlamps in the "up" position when washing the car? (Read your Owner's Manual on the "correct" way to leave them up to wash them).<P>.. GM never installed cup holders, but they had them in just about every other model vehicle for that year?<P>.. GM made the car so @$%& low? Did they ever consider an ATM, or drive up window? Geesh ..<P>.. GM puts the spare tire in the front, but when you get a flat it has to go in the back? What if you are on a trip, and have the trunk loaded with items?<P>.. GM did make a pop-up sunroof air deflector? Isn't a pain to have to take the glass out, then take the deflector out, put the glass in the front, then the deflector in the back?<P>.. GM made an A/C panel that barely lights up at night? Can anyone see those push buttons without staring directly at them? If you're at any angle, forget about seeing them lit.<P>Ever wonder about any of these? Naw - me neither. ; )<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||12
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||11-02-2001||09:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Little Duce Coupe:<BR><B> Did the designers realize that although the little "plastic" car they designed would take greats amount of bad mouthing (still does) would set the industry standard for using materials other than metal in the skin of cars and for standardizing the skeletal framing model.<BR>Is that where Saturn got the idea.. Hhmmmm...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was all part of GM's evil plan.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mattyman||11-02-2001||11:10 PM||||Well, I have no trouble with my manual windows.  Im 6'6 and my arms reach over to the other side, I still have to lean quite a bit though.  Kinda gets annoying.  And I think that extra cutout thing is stupid.  Sometimes I just wonder if people can actually think at all and if they do, What the heck are they thinking?||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroFanaticus2||11-02-2001||11:27 PM||||probably a dumb question, but I have to ask anyway.<P>Maybe that extra cut out in the instrument gauge bezel is for foreign conversions, where for some odd reason the odometer might be on the other side of the cluster??<P>Hell,  they put the steering wheel on the opposite side, and drive on the opposite side.  It's a possibility.||||reg||1
