Z||000009||Posthumane||11-03-2001||12:56 AM||||The shift light is in not in the spot he's reffering to. He's talking about the odometer shaped cutout on the other side of the dash (i think). Maybe they were planning on putting something there in later models. Or maybe the dash was used for other gm models that had something there.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Flamberge||11-03-2001||02:06 AM||||I name all of my Fieros (I'm weird) and so I put the name there with a label maker that resembles the odometer (white letters on black) and it looks acceptable. There is nothing else there, they just wanted symmetry. <P>My biggest Hmmmmm... about the Fiero is why the heck aren't the headlamp covers connected directly onto the lamps themselves? I have had so many problems with that fact in all three of my fieros... 1) After awhile, the covers won't go down flush, and stick up a little. 2) sometimes the lamp won't go up as far and won't push up the cover very far (this happened in my 85 SE.) My current problem (that I haven't fixed, but will) is that the left headlamp isn't "strong" enough to lift the cover, so it needs my help. also to turn them off, same thing. If it had been built like *every* other pop-up headlight car on earth, none of the above would really be a problem, at least not in the context of this post. (My friend had a Porsche 924 that I would always blow away, but one thing he had over me was that *his* headlights were connected to their covers.)<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||11-03-2001||02:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Little Duce Coupe:<BR><B>Is that where Saturn got the idea.. Hhmmmm...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes.  Not only is that where Saturn got the idea, but Saturn's dent resistant body panels are the same material as the Fiero body (or very close) and the material is made with the same equipment that was used in the Fiero plant.  So the next Saturn you see has body panels that were made by the same machines that made the body panels on your Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||11-03-2001||02:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AutoXdbdragSE:<BR><B>my 84 has a shift light, i've never really payed attention to where it is??  so.. it might actually be there, i only have one unused gap in my cluster and it's one of the checkengine style openings</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All 4 cylinder sticks have a shift light in the idiot light cluster.  Top right, I believe.  The lens is there on my Formula, but it's not hooked up to anything.  V6 5-speeds didn't have the shift light, presumably because the people buying V6 Fieros aren't as interested in fuel economy. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Little Duce Coupe||11-03-2001||02:29 AM||||This is great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>..I don't know how to cut and paste yet but we'll try from memory, :O<P>--They did intall cup holders.. there is one on each side of the back of the pod.  The one on the left is for large cups and the one on the right is for medium.<P>--So we can now conclude the engineers were at least 6' or more.<P>--You mean the little trick of shutting the lights off and "quickly" turning the running lights back on?<P>--If you get a flat (or two in one weekend in my case) your wife holds the lugage and no I don't have a luggage rack for the back.<P>--Yep.. my 88' has a shift light.. but if your really pay attention to it you can't keep up with a ford Escort (pre 90).<P>--Whew.. bought mine used and always thought my my panel lights were just bad.<P>--Actually.. California has BIG mountains and I have driven in the snow..very spooky in a Fiero and I crashed deep puddles (contrary to opinion it does rain in calif.)<BR>that were above my door sills and the window always clears with in a couple o minutes.<P>--I know the spare tire fits in the trunk because I gave my wifer her choice.. tire or lugage.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>--I wish I had a sunroof.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I tell myself it will be a classic because I don't want to part with it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||12
